import{_ as t,o as s,c as o,ae as r}from"./chunks/framework.DQC_QtFV.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Logs","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/guide/console/logs.md","filePath":"en/guide/console/logs.md","lastUpdated":1793162416000}'),a={name:"en/guide/console/logs.md"};function n(i,e,l,d,c,h){return s(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="logs" tabindex="-1">Logs <a class="header-anchor" href="#logs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Logs&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The logs page is two views over the same records, chosen by the toolbar&#39;s first control and kept in the URL:</p><ul><li><strong>按轮次</strong> (by turn): one turn reads as one trajectory - its own record opens it (the chat input it rendered and why the turn started: mention, join_in, wait, schedule, free), and its steps follow in append order. The list answers newest first, so one trajectory is read from its end backwards.</li><li><strong>列表</strong> (list): the flat feed, newest first.</li></ul><p>Filters by kind (turn, assistant, tool_call, tool_result, send, note_write, note_replace, note_delete, rollover, reminder, jev, error, system), by source (driver, bot, console), by conversation and by turn.</p><p>One tool call and its result read as one step, with the arguments, the result and the duration; a <code>code_exec</code> result also lists each nested call its script made with its status - the only place a nested call&#39;s outcome lives. A model call&#39;s token use rides on its own step. A send record lists its bubbles with the state the driver reported for each (sent, queued, failed, not_attempted), completed as the driver reports them.</p><p>A jev record carries its probabilities, and a decision that ships in shadow also carries what it would have done. The join-in gate rides on the turn&#39;s own record: the probability, the penalty with its factors (a recent reply, how much of the talk was mine, low talkativeness, a quiet time of day), the threshold, the score and the decision in the bot&#39;s own words. A batch held by the idle backoff has its own record with the backoff that was applied.</p><p>Entries stream in live; after a restart the recent history is seeded once from the bot and the stream resumes, de-duplicated by record id. The panel&#39;s own events - logins, sticker deletes, driver errors, live-view sessions - are folded into the same list with source console.</p>',7)])])}const w=t(a,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,w as default};
